{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457304-v20-mortal-hunter-creation-mistake","id":1457304,"title":"[V20] Mortal Hunter Creation Mistake?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-20T16:35:29-07:00","id":1457304,"title":"[V20] Mortal Hunter Creation Mistake?","content":"So in The Hunters Hunters 2 on page 35 the character creation rules says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prioritize the three categories: Talents, Skills, Knowledges (13/9/5). </div> </div> </div>However, on the character sheet in the back of the book says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abilities 11/7/4 </div> </div> </div>So my question is, which of this is correct? This is in the final version of the PDF so this mistake is obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T17:57:27-07:00","id":1457307,"title":"","content":"The second one.<br /> <br /> Hunter's Hunted use mortal creation rules, in WoD they give 11/7/4 to mortals, while 13/9/5 is for supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Personally I always go with 13/9/5 anyways when I'm the ST, to me this is it for PCs, but the canonical rule is with lower numbers for mortals.<br /> <br /> You can clarify by looking at the Attribute spread. If it follows the supernatural spread (7/5/3), it is the first option, if follows the mortal spread (6/4/3 IIRC), the second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T02:18:56-07:00","id":1457374,"title":"","content":"I believe it always been 6/4/3 for Attributes and 11/7/4 for Abilities. It makes sense. Remember what Louis said about his transformation in &quot;Interview with a vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;My senses were sharper&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> During my games I've always used the spread as described above for every mortal character (with the exception for shapeshifters before First Change, they always have 7/5/3) adding the missing dots after the Embrace/Awakening/Chrysalis (for shapeshifters only Abilities of course). But I've also heavily changed the character's creation and advancement:<br /> first of all my players don't use character sheet. Instead they get a list of traits (mostly physical) that their characters can inherit from their parents and grandparents. Some of those traits comes from their ancestors and mark them as &quot;genetically supernaturals&quot; (that means they could be p. ex. shapeshifters). If they take enough of those traits they will become the creature which traits they have. Of course they could choose not to inherit specific traits and choose others that their parents don't have. If most of the traits are from &quot;ordinary&quot; mortals they will play mortals unless they get a chance to become something more (Embraced, forcibly Awaken or something like that). There's also a chance to become Wraiths, determined randomly and by their style of play. It could of course put me in a situation that one character is a bastet, three others are mortals and one wraith, but that could be interesting. As for freebies and XP they fill the charts with their characters school grades, police and medical databases and psychological evaluation. Using those I fill the character sheets so they don't know for sure what their characters really capable of. As for XP they declare what their characters do in their free time (or if they used some traits frequently during play) I modify their character's stats accordingly. Only one thing they know: living characters (shapeshifters, Mages, mortals etc) can modify their stats as they want, dead ones (vampires, mummies, demons) cannot upgrade their attributes (it's hard to change the dead body) unless they use some magical methods (Vicissitude, help from mages or something like that). The only exeption are Wraiths, they can modify their Corpus (physical stats, appearance and perception) freely","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T09:30:16-07:00","id":1457401,"title":"","content":"I ended up looking more into it, and found out that the premade characters from the same book use the first option (13/9/5). I guess they tried to make hunters on par with vamps in 20th, or they made the mistake early in writing and never changed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T12:21:28-07:00","id":1457414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457304-v20-mortal-hunter-creation-mistake?p=1457401#post1457401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up looking more into it, and found out that the premade characters from the same book use the first option (13/9/5). I guess they tried to make hunters on par with vamps in 20th, or they made the mistake early in writing and never changed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or these are not mere untrained mortals but hunters with some experience. Substract dots from comber abilities and see what would happen (this of course would prove my theory \ud83d\ude08).<br /> <br /> And of course remember that mortals have more freebies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 08-22-2021, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T13:04:12-07:00","id":1457417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457304-v20-mortal-hunter-creation-mistake?p=1457414#post1457414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or these are not mere untrained mortals but hunters with some experience. Substract dots from comber abilities and see what would happen (this of course would prove my theory \ud83d\ude08).<br /> <br /> And of course remember that mortals have more freebies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually checked for freebie points. They have the 13/9/5 spread with 21 freebie points spent. That said, the sheet also says they should have 15 freebie points, so that would also be a mistake if we go by sheet is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:27:17-07:00","id":1457441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457304-v20-mortal-hunter-creation-mistake?p=1457417#post1457417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually checked for freebie points. They have the 13/9/5 spread with 21 freebie points spent. That said, the sheet also says they should have 15 freebie points, so that would also be a mistake if we go by sheet is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still believe it's a typo. Or some of the freebies were spent according to the character concept (but I doubt it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T16:42:56-07:00","id":1457526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457304-v20-mortal-hunter-creation-mistake?p=1457401#post1457401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up looking more into it, and found out that the premade characters from the same book use the first option (13/9/5). I guess they tried to make hunters on par with vamps in 20th, or they made the mistake early in writing and never changed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not rely too much in the premades, 'cause they're not always conforming to the rules. I do agree with Nail Eater that this seems to be a typo.<br /> <br /> But again and more importantly, don't overthink it. Applying the same rule across the board for your players is far more important than following so precisely this spread.<br /> <br /> It is literally something that won't hurt your game in the list, no matter how you look at it, unless you would want to mess with the numbers anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T07:14:55-07:00","id":1457574,"title":"","content":"Frankly, Hunters are so far behind Vampires in terms of basic abilities that even if you used 7/5/3 Attributes, 13/9/5 Abilities, 7 Virtues, 5 Backgrounds and 21 Freebies they\u2019d still be far enough behind vampires (no soak lethal/bashing does half/torpor if not aggravated, no blood pool and its stat-bumping and quick healing, no free 3 dots in disciplines) that they\u2019d still face an uphill battle with even a 13th Gen neonate.<br /> <br /> The mortal stat arrays are basically just dropping an extra layer of suck onto the non-primary supernaturals so you\u2019ll mostly stick with vamps, wolves and mages instead of ghouls/revenants/hunters, kinfolk and sorcerers/consors.<br /> <br /> In any sort of mixed game, I\u2019d give all the non-primary types the same arrays as vamp/wolf/mages if they\u2019re PCs. This goes double when Vampire PCs are involved in the mix since their rather strict limitations on vampire PCs\u2019 daylight activities will end up dragging everyone else into nighttime exclusive activity cycles so as not to exclude that PC from the bulk of the game and, thus, the primary advantage of those mortal types over vampires (daylight activity/sun immunity) won\u2019t actually be an advantage because their players won\u2019t want to be dicks to the vampire players.<br /> <br /> ETA: the daytime limits on WoD vampires are so extreme that the last time we did a crossover we actually rewrote the rules so they didn\u2019t suffer from daysleep and only direct sunlight did damage and it still affected how all the other players had to plan their character\u2019s actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 08-24-2021, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T22:58:23-07:00","id":1457689,"title":"","content":"If you want to use the first one, use the first one. If there is clearly some ambiguity (and this happens in the rules) then the ST can interpret it how they please and it probably can be rationalized. I'd agree with the others about the 'mortal vs supernatural' ability definition otherwise, but you could argue that a mortal that had 13/9/5 represented a 'blessed' or especially lucky human... someone touched by supernatural forces in ways more subtle than might be represented by Numina, say.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I say it comes down to what works for you and your game and there's no reason to look for justifications for it. It's a YMMV issue. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}